{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>You shall not abominate an Edomite.</b> Some explain: even though they did not precede you, you shall not abominate them, for he is your brother and of the seed of Abraham. And accordingly, one must read 'who dealt with me' as 'the children of Esau dealt with me,' referring to the matter of passing through their land, as it is written regarding Jephthah: ״וישלח ישראל מלאכים אל מלך מואב לאמר אעברה בארצך ולא אבה וגם אל מלך אדום שלח ולא אבה.״ Alternatively: you shall not abominate an Edomite — even though you had reason to abominate him, because he did not let you pass through his land — you shall not abominate him, for he is your brother." "<b>You shall not abominate an Egyptian.</b> Even though in the end they enslaved you, you shall not abominate them, for you were a stranger in his land and they did good to you at first."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:19.202352024Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}